<title>GERMANY: Siemens -led group wins Brazil rail order.</title>
<headline>Siemens -led group wins Brazil rail order.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by Siemens AG and including Japan's Mitsui Group has won a 100 million mark contract to deliver 10 electric trains to Sao Paolo, Siemens said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Each train, equipped with three-phase traction technology, will seat about 885 passengers and reach top speeds of 90 km/h.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
